note: E4-017
note: A field's default value is worked out by the engine each time an object is made, as part of making that object.
note: A default that makes another object of the same class therefore never finishes making the first one. A program's own
note: calls would stop at the call depth limit; this nests inside the engine instead, and the native stack budget ends it.
class Node do:
    any next = Node()
end
Node first = Node()
print("unreachable")
